e of ned stark's  execution at the hands of sadistic  incest baby king joffrey baratheon king  in the north rob stark marches south for  vengeance in order to build his army and  secure passage across a crucial river  rob enters into a strategic marriage  though he's promised to one of the many  many daughters of important ally walder  frey rob strays off the path set for him  by his mother and marries to lisa with  whom he has fallen in love walder frey  puts on a brave face about the whole  thing and accepts ed mertoli for one of  his daughters instead secretly though he  aligns himself with the lannisters and  boltons and plans to wipe out the starks  as edmure and his bride are taken to  their wedding bed walter frey locks the  doors behind rob catlin and talisa  they're all brutally killed soon after  the lannisters and their records  the scene and house of the dragon isn't  quite as dramatically bloody as the red  wedding but there's a distinct  similarity that can't be overlooked just  as walder frey settles for edmure lord  corliss velaryon and his wife reynise  originally want to marry their daughter  to viserys but settle for their son  becoming king consort to the presumed  future queen instead clearly bad things  happen when people don't get their first  choice
 

